  "shortDescription": "Aid us in keeping our community bright and strong for the future.",
  "projectStory": "Project story\nCreator\nKirstie Lindsay\nmore infocontact\nCategory\nLocal Businesses\nTags\nother\nBacking information\nCrowdfunding risks\nlearn more\nWe started as an idea by some parents and teachers at Elwick Community School who wanted a place to meet, share ideas, and have access to some basic resources. At first all we had was a room in the school that people could meet in once in a while but over the last 17 years this small idea has blossomed and grown into a vital, meaningful part of the community. What was once just an idea has become a grass roots independent not for profit and we are in danger of losing our ability to continue to provide the level and quality of resources and programs to the people who matter most, all of you.\nWe are a safe, nurturing, welcoming place for families and individuals to access all sorts of resources from basic food security through our “Helping Hands Pantry” to social well-being through our “Empowering Yourself Everyday” (E.Y.E.) Series Workshops. To see more of the sorts of programs we run, photos etc please check out our website at www.elwickvillage.org  \nYou can be a part of keeping this centre alive and vibrant.\nSo brass tacks what we need is $60,000 plus dollars to keep the place running. The reason why is because one of our funders for the last three years was a short term provincial government program that is ending this March. We didn’t do anything wrong, the community isn’t in less need or any less worthy, the funds just no longer exist.\nWhat do you get for donating? Well beyond the obvious benefits of being able to help out this great organization and being an awesome human being you will receive some great perks that you can see on the side here.\nEveryone who donates even $1 will get a special thank you on our website and in our social media. For those able to do a little more we have some really great things including gifts from some of our artist friends out there in the world Chris Walters, Ursula Neufeld and Nereo ll.\nOne of the great things about this campaign is that even if we do not reach our complete goals here on IndieGoGo every dime donated will still be used for exactly what we are proposing. We will use that money to keep the place going at full strength and keep searching for sustainable funding.\nWhat it means if we don’t find new funds\nProgramming will be cut from 6 days a week to 3 or 4 partial days\nLess access to essential needs such as food and clothing\nLess access to outside resources\nLess access to advocacy and capacity building\nLess programming\n            · for families\n            · for children\n            · for youth\n            · for crime prevention\n            · for personal empowerment\nIf you aren’t able to give monetarily that is ok you can still help out. Spread the word; tell your friends and family, share about us on Facebook and other social media, donate a piece of artwork or time in a class you are teaching that we can offer as a perk, like us on Facebook, check out our website, swing by for a coffee and tell us that Elwick Village matters. We are looking forward to continuing to be a vibrant part of this great community for a long time to come.\nAt Elwick Village & Resource Centre, we consider ourselves and the centre to be a safe, welcoming and nurturing environment and an LGBT Ally. This means that we recognize that difference, in all its forms enriches our community and we reject types of discrimination. We respect and welcome all persons, regardless of their age, culture, race, religion, perceived or actual sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression.\nAbove photo is of the perk original artwork by Nereo ll\nAbove photo are some samples of the hand painted reusable tote bags and T-shirt designed and made by the kids of Elwick Village. There are 3 options to receive one or more of these items as a perk for your donation  :)\n\n\nStay tuned for more photos of some of the other perks to come...",
